────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

This project contains a fork of Immich (https://github.com/immich-app/immich),
copyright the Immich contributors, also licensed under AGPL-3.0. The forked
code lives in immich/ — principally the web client (immich/web) and the mobile
app (immich/mobile) — and has been modified to talk to a Cloudflare Worker
backed by Telegram storage instead of the upstream Immich server.

If you want a conventional self-hosted photo server on your own hardware, use
Immich itself. It is excellent, and this project would not exist without it.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The Drive web app in drive-web/ is derived from the frontend of File Browser
(https://github.com/filebrowser/filebrowser), commit
e8a388f840173580116f2743813d03b22286e44e (v2.63.23), copyright the File
Browser contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy
of that license is in drive-web/LICENSE.filebrowser. Upstream shipped no
NOTICE file and no per-file notices at that commit.

The upstream files were imported unmodified in their own commit; every later
change is in the git history. Files we changed carry a header saying so.
JSON files cannot hold a comment, so the ones we changed are listed in
drive-web/MODIFIED.md instead. "File Browser" is the upstream project's name;
this app does not use its name or logos as its own brand, and credits it as
"Based on File Browser". The build writes the licences of everything bundled
into the app to THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt, served beside it.

